ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FIGURE & FORM DUO WORKSHOP","url":"https://www.meetup.com/advance-photographic-workshops/events/316470300/","description":"We will be creating some beautiful artistic sets with Ciara and Kalopsia, some creative and beatiful sets with some of the best creative models in the country. We will be doing duo creative sets with both models to add some unique images to your portfolio.\n\nTo find out more about the studio and workshop you can visit [https://www.productionstudio.ca](https://www.productionstudio.ca)\n\nThis is a [ticketed](https://www.productionstudio.ca/purchase) event, Secure your spot today!\n\n**Who Should Attend?**\nOur workshops at The Production Studio are designed for photographers looking to expand their skills or build their portfolios in a professional setting. Whether you’re a beginner or an experienced shooter, these sessions offer hands-on learning with top-tier talent from leading agencies.\n\nStudio photography can feel intimidating, but our workshops provide a relaxed environment where you can observe, ask questions, and learn by doing. There’s nothing like hands on experience.\n\nWith a variety of styles and themes, each session ensures participants have the opportunity to shoot one-on-one with models, refine their techniques, and connect with fellow photographers and enthusiasts.\n\n**​ What you should bring:**\n\n* A DSLR/Mirrorless camera\n* Fully Charged Battery\n* Freshly Formatted Memory Card(s)\n* General Lenses: 24-70mm, 24-105mm and 70-200mm If you have a macro lens, 50mm or 85mm please bring it along. It really depends on the type of workshop\n* Pocket Wizards (if you have your own, otherwise one will be provided for you)\n* Bring along a list of shots you’d like to achieve or posing ideas. It can help to ensure that you get the perfect image.\n\n**Workshop Details:**\n\n* ​Arrival: Upon arrival, use the intercom to call unit 205 for entry. Please aim to arrive 15 minutes early to settle in before the session begins.\n* Social Interaction: Feel free to connect with the workshop host and fellow photographers. Keep conversations lighthearted and professional to foster a creative and welcoming environment.\n* Photoshoot Session: Each workshop runs for 3 hours, with participants working one-on-one with the model across 4-5 different sets. The goal is to capture a few standout images from each setup that you can proudly showcase on your website and social media.\n* Model Release: A non-commercial model release, signed by the model, will be provided to each photographer. Photos and videos taken during the workshop can be used for personal promotional purposes only, including portfolios, websites, and print media such as postcards.\n* Please note that behind-the-scenes (BTS) content may be captured by individuals, the model, MUA, or the event host. If you prefer not to be recorded, kindly inform everyone before the event begins.\n\n**Cancellation Policy**\nCancellations are accepted 7-14 days before the workshop (depending on the event) for a full refund. This policy ensures workshops can run smoothly for the studio, models, and MUAs.\n\nThink of workshop registration like purchasing a concert ticket, refunds aren’t typically given. However, if you cancel within 7 days and a replacement is found, a full refund will be issued.\n\nIf the organizer cancels, you’ll receive a full refund. In rare cases, a model may be replaced due to illness, but only with someone of similar look and talent.\n\n**About the organizer:**\nEmanuel Pires has been a photographer for over a decade, leading more than 800 workshops. With years of experience, he offers professional, engaging, and educational sessions designed to inspire creativity. His goal is to build a vibrant community of artists, models, and makeup artists within his professional space.\n\n​To learn more about Emanuel, visit his website [Pires Photography](https://www.piresphotography.ca).\n\nThis is a [ticketed](https://www.productionstudio.ca/purchase) event, Secure your spot today!","startDate":"2026-10-25T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"142 Cawthra Ave","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"142 Cawthra Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Advance Photographic Workshops","url":"https://www.meetup.com/advance-photographic-workshops/"},"performer":"Advance Photographic Workshops"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂🌿 NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park 🌿🍂","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316183922/","description":"# 🍂🌿 **NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park** 🌿🍂\n\n### A Brand-New Toronto Park, Fall Colours & Waterfront Trails\n\nWe're trying something **new**!\n\nJoin us for our first group walk to **Biidaasige Park**, one of the newest and most ambitious parks in Toronto. Opened as part of the massive transformation of the Port Lands, the park sits on **Ookwemin Minising**, Toronto's new island where the Don River meets Lake Ontario.\n\nThis isn't a walk we've done before, which makes it a little more exciting. We'll spend much of the afternoon actually **exploring the park rather than rushing through it** — following its trails, enjoying the waterfront, taking in the fall scenery, and stopping along the way to appreciate the new landscape.\nThe park is enormous, with more than **50 acres already open** and more sections being added as the Port Lands transformation continues.\n\nThere are curated trails and paths, viewpoints, natural areas, and places to get down closer to the new Don River.\nAnd because we're doing this in the fall, we'll get to experience the park at a completely different time of year — cooler air, changing leaves, open skies, and fewer summer crowds. 🍂\n\nWe'll meet at the **Young Centre in the Distillery District** simply because it's an easy and convenient meeting point before we head toward the park. We won't be spending the day touring the Distillery District — **the park is the destination.**\n\n📲 **Don't Forget to join our WhatsApp Group – [\\[CLICK HERE!\\]](http://xn--[click%20here!](%20join%20our%20whatsapp%20group-cu832c:%20Click%20here%20to%20join)/)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ **What We'll Do**\n\nWe'll meet outside the **Young Centre for the Performing Arts** and make our way toward Biidaasige Park.\nOnce we reach the park, we'll slow things down and spend about **90 minutes exploring the trails and waterfront**.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* 🍂 Enjoy the fall colours\n* 🌿 Explore the park's trails and green spaces\n* 🌊 Walk along the new waterfront landscape\n* 📸 Stop for photos and scenic views\n* 🌳 Explore the natural areas around the new Don River\n* 🌆 Take in views toward the Toronto skyline and Toronto Islands\n* 🚶‍♂️ Enjoy plenty of time to walk and talk with the group\n\nThe walk itself will be approximately **2 hours**, but we're not trying to race through it.\n**This is about experiencing the park.**\nIt's our first time doing this walk, so we'll take our time and actually enjoy discovering what has been created here.\n\n***\n\n## 🌊 **Why Biidaasige Park?**\n\nBiidaasige Park is part of one of the biggest transformations Toronto has seen in decades.\nThe new Don River was created as part of the Port Lands Flood Protection project, transforming former industrial land into a new river valley, wetlands, parkland and public spaces.\n\nThe first phase of Biidaasige Park opened in July 2025.\nThe park includes **accessible trails, cycling paths, river access, wetlands, viewpoints and waterfront promenades**, with views toward the Toronto Islands, Inner Harbour and skyline.\n\nAnd there's something particularly fun about visiting a place that is still **brand new**.\nWe're not revisiting an old Toronto favourite.\n**We're discovering somewhere new together.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍺 **After the Walk: The Keating Channel Pub & Grill**\n\nAfter exploring the park, we'll head over to **The Keating Channel Pub & Grill** for lunch.\nThe pub sits right on the Keating Channel and has been a local fixture in the area for more than 20 years. After years of Port Lands construction made the neighbourhood difficult to reach, the transformation of the area has brought new life and new visitors back to the waterfront.\nIt's a nice way to finish the day: **a brand-new park followed by one of the neighbourhood's old survivors.**\nLunch is optional, but everyone is welcome to join us.\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 **Fall Weather & Expectations**\n\nThis is a **social urban walk**, not a difficult hike.\nWe'll be walking for approximately two hours, including our time exploring the park, so you should be comfortable being on your feet for that length of time.\nPlease dress for typical Toronto fall weather. The waterfront can be cooler and windier than other parts of the city, so a warm layer is a good idea.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 **Meetup Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside the **Young Centre for the Performing Arts**, 50 Tank House Lane, in the Distillery District. Young Centre for the Performing Arts\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** The Keating Channel Pub & Grill\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ **Meetup Fee**\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing walks and events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 **What to Bring**\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n📸 Your phone or camera for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 **Who Is This For?**\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy discovering new places in Toronto\n* Anyone who likes parks and waterfront trails\n* People who want a relaxed social walk\n* Anyone interested in seeing Toronto's newest public spaces\n* People who enjoy exploring somewhere they've never been before\n* Anyone who wants to spend a fall day outside with good people\n\nThe park may be new.\n**The idea is the same: come out, walk with us, and meet some people along the way.**\n\n***\n\n📲 **You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time — or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.**\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come discover a new park.**\n**Stay for the fall colours.**\n**Stay a little longer for lunch and friendship.** 🍂🌿🍺","startDate":"2026-10-25T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Young Centre for the Performing Arts","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Distillery District, 50 Tank House Lane, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/316231810/","description":"Welcome to the Sunday meetup for Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games, and have fun while doing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we will add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like to post for\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\, include the name of the game\\, number of players needed for the game\\, whether you are offering a teach or not\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already been posted\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\, we respectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event","startDate":"2026-10-25T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/"},"performer":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Franchise Canada Show Toronto — Fall 2026 (Sunday)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tech-hangout/events/315999079/","description":"Ready to become your own boss—but don’t want to build a business entirely on your own?\nJoin fellow entrepreneurs, business builders, and opportunity seekers at the **Franchise Canada Show Toronto — Fall 2026**, Canada’s premier franchise exhibition. This free event brings leading franchise brands, experienced operators, and industry experts together under one roof at the Toronto Congress Centre.\nWhether you’re actively exploring business ownership or simply curious about franchising, this is an opportunity to discover proven business models, compare investment options, and get practical guidance directly from the people who know the industry best.\n\n## What you’ll discover\n\n**Explore franchise opportunities across 60+ sectors**\nMeet representatives from established brands and emerging concepts in food, technology, beauty, construction, professional services, retail, and more. Explore opportunities at a wide range of investment levels and find options that match your experience, ambitions, and budget.\n**Speak directly with industry experts**\nConnect face-to-face with franchisors, successful franchisees, and experienced professionals. Ask candid questions, understand the realities of ownership, and gain insights that can help you make a confident, informed decision.\n**Attend free educational seminars**\nLearn about financing, legal considerations, marketing, operations, franchise selection, and other essential aspects of building a successful franchise business. Hear practical strategies and real-world lessons from people who have already made the journey.\n\n## Why attend?\n\nSince 1996, the Canadian Franchise Association has helped thousands of Canadians explore business ownership through credible franchise systems. The Franchise Canada Show is the CFA’s official exhibition and one of the best places to begin—or accelerate—your search.\nCome prepared to learn, make valuable connections, and discover what your next chapter could look like.\n**Get into business for yourself—but not by yourself.**\nAttendance is free, but advance registration is encouraged. Reserve your place through the official Eventbrite listing:\n**[Register for the Franchise Canada Show Toronto](https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/franchise-canada-show-toronto-fall-2026-tickets-1989674641413?aff=oddtdtcreator)**\n**Location:** Toronto Congress Centre, Hall F, Toronto, Ontario\n**Official organizer:** Canadian Franchise Association / Franchise Canada Show\n*Please note: LeaderSHIFT and Toronto Tech Hangout are sharing this opportunity with their communities and are not the official event organizers.*\n**Questions or Concerns?**\nNeed support with your LeaderSHIFT Meetup experience? [Submit a support request](https://tally.so/r/68zJZo).","startDate":"2026-10-25T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Congress Centre","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"650 Dixon Road, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Tech Hangout","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tech-hangout/"},"performer":"Toronto Tech Hangout"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"In-Person Writing Sprints","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/events/316740744/","description":"Struggling with motivation and focus as you hammer away on your manuscript at home? Want to join a community of writers as we embrace the joys and pains (mostly pains) of writing together?\n\nBring your laptop, pen & paper, old-school typewriter, or futuristic writing gadget, and join an enthusiastic community of science fiction and fantasy writers as we work on our current projects in the same space. The format will be similar to our online writing sprints: 30-minute blocks of focused, quiet writing time (the sprints), interspersed with breaks where we can chat, ask questions, and share our writing experiences.","startDate":"2026-10-25T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"MaRS Discovery District","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"101 College St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Special Event: Autumn hike through Mt. Pleasant Cemetary to Brickworks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/riverdale-5k/events/316771405/","description":"A spooky hike where we can enjoy the changing leaves in full autumn.\n\nWe will start with an inspirational walk through Mt. Pleasant Cemetary and then continuing on to the Brickworks to enjoy the remainder of the changing leaves through the Moore Ravine.\n\n**When:** Sunday, October 25, start at 1:30pm\n**Where:** Gather by the entrance on Yonge St. ([https://maps.app.goo.gl/Shqzx7fxMCBQvWJy8](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Shqzx7fxMCBQvWJy8), south of Davisville Station).\n\n**Mt. Pleasant Cemetery:** ([https://www.mountpleasantgroup.com/Locations/Cemeteries/Mount-Pleasant.aspx](https://www.mountpleasantgroup.com/Locations/Cemeteries/Mount-Pleasant.aspx \"https://www.mountpleasantgroup.com/Locations/Cemeteries/Mount-Pleasant.aspx\"))\n\n**Evergreen Brickworks:**\nhttps://www.evergreen.ca/stories/your-ultimate-fall-guide-to-evergreen-brick-works/\n\nSend me a direct message if you have any questions.","startDate":"2026-10-25T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Riverdale Park 5K","url":"https://www.meetup.com/riverdale-5k/"},"performer":"Riverdale Park 5K"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Music Bingo with Friends! (Best of 7 Decades!)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316602447/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\nI'd like to invite you out to a fun-filled afternoon with this fantastic social game called **MUSIC BINGO with Friends! (Best of 7 Decades!)**\n\nEveryone can play (It's easy to learn and most of all it's a lot of fun!)\n\n\\*Joined by my other social groups too; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out\n\n\\*Please note we are at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we are in the back dining area to find us)**\n\n*\\*You can also ask the wait staff or bartender if you like to show you to the group (simply ask for Steve's games event)*\n\nEvent Details Below:\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Details of Event:**\n**Music Bingo with Friends! (Best of 7 Decades!)**\n\nMusic Bingo puts a fun musical twist on traditional bingo. Instead of listening for numbers, you'll hear familiar songs from across the decades and mark them off on your Music Bingo card.\n\nYou don't need to be a music expert — recognizing the songs, singing along and enjoying the company is all part of the fun!\n\n• **Seven decades of great music** with plenty of familiar favourites\n• **Treats for our winning participants** during the different rounds\n• **Meet and mingle** with a friendly group while enjoying a relaxed social atmosphere\n• **Come on your own or invite some friends** — we'll get everyone settled in and ready to play\n\n**Event Fee: $10**\nYour event fee includes **Music Bingo, treats for our winners, reserved seating and plenty of music, laughs and fun throughout the event.**\nPayment can be made **in cash at the event** or **in advance by e-transfer to [SteveFlemming11@gmail.com](mailto:SteveFlemming11@gmail.com)**.\nIf paying by e-transfer, please include **your name** in the message so your payment can be easily identified.\n\nBring your music memories, your sense of humour and maybe even your singing voice — although singing along is completely optional!\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\nPlease arrive between **2:00 PM and 2:30 PM** so you'll have time to get settled, meet some people and get ready to play. **Music Bingo will begin shortly afterward.**\n\n\\*Great lunch menu and food specials provided:\n(One beverage or appetizer minimum upon arrival to support venue)\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\\*Lots of street parking on avenue and free residential parking\n[https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/](https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/)\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge & Lawrence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)","startDate":"2026-10-25T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1999 Avenue Rd, North York, ON M5M 4A5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Singles Pickleball Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cinders/events/316754871/","description":"Skip the awkward first dates and come for a fun, social afternoon of pickleball & drinks with other singles 💓\n\n**Important:**\n**RSVP’ing on Meetup does not reserve your spot.**\n**To join this experience, you must sign up through [app.cinders.dating](https://app.cinders.dating/eventDetails?eventRef=j2ZrcGCWANVplf6nfDs9). Only confirmed guests will receive the exact location and details.**\n\nEvery month, we curate singles with similar hobbies, interests and profiles and invite them to join a group experience built around an activity.\n\n🥒🎾 **This month, we are doing pickleball**!\n\n**Details**\n🎾 Rotate through casual pickleball games, meet different people, hang out and have a drink between matches. Beginners welcome.\n\n🏆 A little friendly competition at the end, with a Cinders perk for the winners.\n\n📍 King East (exact meeting location will be shown to confirmed guests)\n📅 Sunday, Oct. 25 at 2pm\n👫 16 people (balanced gender)\n🎟️ Ticketed experience. Includes access to a pickleball court.\n\n**How to sign up**\n**[Sign up through cinders.dating](https://app.cinders.dating/eventDetails?eventRef=j2ZrcGCWANVplf6nfDs9). Only confirmed guests will receive the location details.**","startDate":"2026-10-25T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Cinders: Fun Activities with Curated Singles","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cinders/"},"performer":"Cinders: Fun Activities with Curated Singles"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-french-conversation-exchange/events/316214195/","description":"This is an informal conversation group for anyone wanting to practice / use their French and meet some new people. All levels are welcome, but having a conversational level is strongly recommended (and of course native French speakers are very welcome too!). / Il s'agit d'un groupe de conversation informel pour toute personne souhaitant pratiquer / utiliser son français et rencontrer de nouvelles personnes. Tous les niveaux sont les bienvenus, mais il est recommandé d'avoir un niveau de conversation approximatif (et bien sûr, les locuteurs natifs du français sont également les bienvenus !)\n\nNous nous rencontrerons dimanche, de 14h00 à 16h00, au foodcourt de Brookfield Place, qui heureusement a beaucoup de tables et garde la musique basse!\n\n+ Juste un rappel que ce groupe est un lieu d'échange détendu avec les autres dans un esprit de respect, de tolérance et de réceptivité à la multiplicité des cultures et des niveaux de français représentés. Merci de respecter ces principes en participant aux meetups.","startDate":"2026-10-25T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Brookfield Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"181 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-french-conversation-exchange/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Island of Dr. Moreau","url":"https://www.meetup.com/more-than-a-classic-book-club/events/316527416/","description":"October is the month where we celebrate all things spooky, dark, and scary. Our novel this month, *The Island of Dr. Moreau*, promises to leave you disturbed - or at least, uncomfortable. It is a powerful, short, philosophical novel examining human cruelty and pain and the moral choices attached to scientific invention. Sound familiar? Written by the father of science fiction, H.G. Wells, in 1896, it explores questions such as, what happens when human intelligence challenges the very structure of nature? Highly accessible, about 115 pages, *The Island of Dr. Moreau* is a famous work that has been adapted to film, audiobooks, and other media.","startDate":"2026-10-25T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Demetres Desserts Distillery District","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"28 Gristmill Lane, Toronto, ON M5A 3C4, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"More Than A Classic Book Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/more-than-a-classic-book-club/"},"performer":"More Than A Classic Book Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sunday Meeple & Gaymes","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/events/315389022/","description":"This is an opportunity to meet up for some LGBTQ2IA-flavoured gaming and socializing—allies also welcome. Come for the gaming, socializing, not to mention One Star's Hot Dog menu! :) Be sure to invite friends and such, too.\n\nAlthough Fred, your amiable host, starts the event at 3pm, feel free to drop in early as One Star opens at 2pm!\n\nYou'll have access to a robust library of board games, and attendees are welcome to bring their own games.\n\nThere is no event fee. Instead we ask attendees to purchase beverages or food from the venue since they are offering us their space for free.\n\nWe provide nametag stickers with a pronoun field; we want this to be a comfortable environment for everyone, kindly respect people's listed or stated pronouns.\n\nIf you are unsure of someone's pronouns, don't assume: Ask, Respect and Practice\nDefinitely ask before taking pictures/videos.\n\nOne Star is NOT an accessible space as the washrooms are down stairs. For those with sensory concerns, there may be possible loud noises. \\*\\*\\*Please reach out to [info@torontogaymers.ca](mailto:info@torontogaymers.ca) with any accessibility concerns.\n[https://linktr.ee/TorontoGaymers](https://linktr.ee/TorontoGaymers)\n\n#TorontoGaymers #OneStarBarTO","startDate":"2026-10-25T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"One Star Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"538 Queen St W, Toronto, ON M5V 2B5, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Gaymers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/"},"performer":"Toronto Gaymers"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/1/6/3/highres_536052643.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/3/8/highres_535740824.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/3/7/3/highres_510977267.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/b/0/b/highres_532059691.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/f/4/a/highres_521328970.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/7/8/b/